{"rationale":"First, we need to determine how many cups of raisins Heather will use for each of the three recipes. Since she divides the bag of raisins equally among the recipes, we divide the total number of cups (27) by 3. Then, we calculate how many batches of oatmeal cookies can be made with the raisins intended for cookies. Each batch of oatmeal cookies takes 3/4 of a cup of raisins. So, we divide the raisins intended for cookies by the amount needed per batch.

Cups of raisins per recipe: 27 / 3 = 9 cups
Batches of oatmeal cookies: 9 / (3/4) = 9 * (4/3) = 12 batches","answer":12}

